    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d30">

                <pb facs="0042" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/1–1149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-11T10:00:00+08:00">January 11,
                            1949—10 a. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 11—12:19 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Shanghai English language press reports Madam Sun Yat-sen statement that all
                    rumors regarding her assuming any office or responsibility in Government [are]
                    without foundation.</p>
                <p>From sources close to Madam Sun we have reason believe press reports correct.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 62, repeated Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
